WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:04.320
Robbie, this new Walkman is absolutely wonderful.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.720
Richard and Marilyn bought it for me for my birthday.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.440
They're so thoughtful.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.280
You are very lucky, Robbie, to have such a nice family.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.500
No, nothing.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.540
Yes, there is.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.240
I can tell.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.560
What's the matter?

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.320
Come on, you can tell me.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.220
What's up?

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:31.760
I don't know.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.360
Something's wrong.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.900
I received a letter from my parents this morning.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.920
Did they write some bad news?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.040
No.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.980
Well, then why are you so sad?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.400
I miss them.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.500
I miss them very much.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.820
I'm sorry, Alexandra.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.700
But I understand.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.900
The Molinas treat me so nicely,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.280
and I love being with your family so much ...

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.500
with photographs of my family, I cried.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.160
I cried because I miss them all.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.880
You really miss your family, don't you?

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.840
It's not like I have nobody.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.200
I like the Molinas very much,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.880
and they're so kind to me.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.580
Hey, why don't we go out

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.460
for a cheeseburger and french fries?

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.660
That'll cheer you up.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.340
And you can use my Walkman.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.980
That's a good idea.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.140
But if we go out,

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.500
please don't complain

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.280
about your math teacher or your math homework.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.820
I want to have fun.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.020
So do I.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.290
I have to turn off the lights,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.340
or else my father will get really angry.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:07.700
He says I never turn them out when I leave.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.980
If they come home and they're on ...

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.680
Do you hear something?

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:16.760
Yes.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.420
What was that?

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.660
It sounded like a dog barking.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.080
It sounded like a dog barking right here.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:24.940
Yeah.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.120
A dog!

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.000
A springer spaniel!

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.350
Come on in!

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.480
Make yourself at home.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:40.350
Come on.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.980
Where did you come from?

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.580
and she belongs to Mr. and Mrs. Levinson.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.200
There's a phone number

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.680
five five five ... eight four four eight.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.000
She's so cute.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:41.500
The number you are calling -- 555-8448 --

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.740
is no longer in service.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.470
The number's no longer in service.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.180
You've lost your family.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.190
We'll find them.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:57.960
Don't worry, Alexandra.
